title: [+ month : month +] Revolution
subtitle: The <span style="color:#8B0000">Communists</span> are launching a revolution!
view-if: not national_congress_seen and ((sov_rg_strength*sov_rg_militancy) >= ((fdc_strength*fdc_militancy) + (abl_strength*abl_militancy) + (ard_strength*ard_militancy) * 2) or (sov_rg_strength*sov_rg_militancy) >= ((army_strength*army_militancy) + (interior_police_militancy*interior_police_strength) * 2) or pcdi_votes >= 50) and soviet_leader = "Stalin"
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.pcdi_strength = Q.sov_rg_strength*Q.sov_rg_militancy;
Q.neutral_strength = Q.rg_strength*Q.rg_militancy;
Q.fascist_strength = (Q.fdc_strength*Q.fdc_militancy) + (Q.abl_strength*Q.abl_militancy) + (Q.ard_strength*Q.ard_militancy);
Q.army_strength = (Q.army_strength*Q.rg_militancy) + (Q.interior_police_strength);
!}

= [+ month : month +] Revolution

# credit to redux for this, btw

Aided by the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CE0000">Communist International</span> and under pressure by [+ soviet_leader +] the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span> has seemingly commenced the revolutionary process. Out of nowhere, a call to general strike is published while radical elements of the <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span> storms key infrastructure points across the country, attempting especially to secure control over arms with which to distribute to local workers. Streetfighting erupts as <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">fascist</span> militias and police forces opposed to the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> attempt to put down their uprisings while further more expansive ones are launched across the country.

Factories are occupied through an initiative of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span>-aligned trade unions and radical elements of the General Confederation of Labour, and <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span>-backed worker councils formed within them, expanding its reach beyond Turin. Local government offices are seized and occupied, leaving the inprompteau worker councils as the only form of governance, while within those councils <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span> and <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guard</span> leaders are elected to direct the ongoing revolution. 

- @psi_supports: The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#ED2855">[+ psi_name +]</span> stands with the revolution!
- @social_fascism: This is madness!

@psi_supports
choose-if: communist_strength >= reformist_strength+labour_strength and not psi_in_government and sov_rg_militancy >= 0.2
unavailable-subtitle: The impromptu revolution is doomed to fail.
on-arrival: psi_revolution = 1; pcdi_relation += 100; ldr_relation -= 100; ul_relation -= 100; ds_relation -= 100; psri_relation -= 100; psu_relation -= 100 if psu_formed; pll_relation -= 100 if pll_formed; ppi_relation -= 100; reformist_dissent += 100;
go-to: pcdi_survives if pcdi_strength + neutral_strength >= fascist_strength; pcdi_crushed if pcdi_strength + neutral_strength < fascist_strength

We mobilize the moderate <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span> against the <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">reactionary</span> militias to defend the worker councils, and join the call to general strike. What's left of our party's <span style="color:#FF6961">reformists</span> leave, unwilling to support a violent means of revolution. 

@social_fascism
go-to: pcdi_survives if pcdi_strength >= fascist_strength; pcdi_crushed if pcdi_strength < fascist_strength

@pcdi_survives

The streetfighting in the streets reaches levels one would expect in a civil war before eventually, the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> seem to remain standing. Police stations are stormed across the country, red flags raised above while forces of the <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">Arditismo</span> and <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#3D3D3D;">Fasci</span> driven out of the cities and into the countryside. Arms are distributed from seized armories to local radical workers, organized into a new fledgling <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Army</span> with one task: the fall of the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">al</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ian</span> monarchy, and the defense of the councils.

<span style="color:#008C45">Regi</span><span style="color:#CFCFCF">o Eser</span><span style="color:#CD212A">cito</span> forces across the country are ordered out of their barracks by the King to quell the uprisings and restore order, only pre-empted in <span style="color:#8B0000">communist</span> strongholds where barracks were stormed by local <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Army</span> contingents. The failure of the <span style="color:#0047AB;">bou</span><span style="color:#FFD700;">rge</span><span style="color:#1E99C5;">ois</span>' first line of defense to suppress this revolutionary attempt has reinvigorated the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span>' efforts.

Now, the question on everyone's minds will be answered - can the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> defend against the full force of the state?

- @neutrality: It would be best to wait the chaos out.
- @pcdi_vs_army: The state is nothing without the support of the workers!

@neutrality
view-if: not spd_revolution
go-to: pcdi_vs_army

By firmly taking a side we would split, as the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> want us to. We will wait the chaos out.

@pcdi_vs_army
view-if: psi_revolution
on-arrival: fascist_strength += army_strength; pcdi_victory = 1 if pcdi_strength > fascist_strength; pcdi_beaten = 1if fascist_strength >= pcdi_strength
go-to: pcdi_aftermath

@pcdi_aftermath

[? if pcdi_victory : The answer seems to be yes, as, somehow, the <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Army</span> drive <span style="color:#008C45">Regi</span><span style="color:#CFCFCF">o Eser</span><span style="color:#CD212A">cito</span> forces back into their barracks which are then besieged and occupied one by one. The flames of civil war have been ignited and the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> are prepared to fight this uphill battle to bring about the dictatorship of the proletariat they so desire. ?]

[? if pcdi_beaten : The answer seems to be no, as, predictably, the <span style="color:#008C45">Regi</span><span style="color:#CFCFCF">o Eser</span><span style="color:#CD212A">cito</span> drive the <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Army</span> forces back into their councils which are then besieged and occupied one by one. The flames of civil war have been ignited but the <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> seem after all to not be ready for what is to come. ?]

- @long_war: The war settles into fixed battle lines.
- @true_pcdi_victory: The <span style="color:#8B0000">Communists</span> emerge victorious!
- @pcdi_crushed: The <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> are crushed.
- @civil_war_if_psi: It is a civil war.

@long_war
view-if: not psi_revolution and (pcdi_strength*0.6) < fascist_strength
on-arrival: long_war = 1

The initial phase of the action ends, and somehow, both sides remain standing.

This will not be a quick coup, but a long civil war. The nation will destroy itself before it can be rebuilt again.

- @game_over: Game over.

@true_pcdi_victory
view-if: not psi_revolution and (pcdi_strength*0.6) >= fascist_strength

The <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Army</span> descends upon Italy, picking off <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">reactionary</span> holdout after <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">reactionary</span> holdout in its crusade against capital. Eventually, it emerges unmistakeably victorious, most of <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span> under its control. After sweeping up the remnants of <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">reactionary</span> forces, the eyes of the <span style="color:#8B0000">Communists</span> turn to us, the very leftists who refused to aid them in their victorious revolution.

Revolution has reached <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span>. Merely no longer on our terms.

- @game_over: Game over.

@civil_war_if_psi
view-if: psi_revolution
on-arrival: not_participating = 1; participating = 0; friendly_king = 0
go-to: civil_war

@pcdi_crushed
view-if: not psi_revolution and (fascist_strength*0.6) >= pcdi_strength
on-arrival: rg_banned = 1; sov_rg_strength *= 0.1; sov_rg_militancy *= 0.4; workers_pcdi *= 0.4; veterans_pcdi *= 0.6; workers_psi *= 0.9; workers_psi *= 0.7 if psi_revolution; workers_pnf += 10; veterans_pnf += 10; workers_ul += 10

The <span style="color:#8B0000">communists</span> are predictably crushed. Worker councils are shuttered and leading conspirators executed. The <span style="color:#c2352b">Red Guards</span> in its entirely is banned, and so are most <span style="color:#8B0000">communist</span> publications. The <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C72F35">PCd'I</span>'s leaders are arrested - those that are not summarily executed, anyway.